# parallel-emerge transcript:
#   out/sessions/20260729-065121-ce11e0/build-pki.rpi5.log   (22025 lines, 1526922 bytes)
# an rpi5 arm64 pki image cross-built 2026-07-29. That build ran portage's PARALLEL
# scheduler (build-rpi5-stage4.sh:3754 `--jobs="${CROSS_EMERGE_JOBS:-1}"`), so unlike the
# serial x86 transcript this stream carries ">>> Jobs: ..." scheduler lines — 1752 of them
# in the full file, alongside 283 ">>> Emerging" lines.
#
# The excerpt was chosen (not synthesised) because these 304 lines contain, in one
# contiguous run, every shape the jobs leg has to handle:
#   * ">>> Jobs: 0 of 0 complete" (an emerge invocation with nothing to do)
#   * ">>> Jobs: N of M complete"                         + Load avg
#   * ">>> Jobs: N of M complete, 1 running"              + Load avg
#   * ">>> Jobs: N of M complete, 1 merge wait"           + Load avg
#   * ">>> Emerging (N of M) <atom>::gentoo for <ROOT>/"  (the ROOT-targeted majority)
#   * ">>> Emerging (N of M) <atom>::gentoo"              (BDEPENDs merged into /)
#   * the ">>> Installing"/">>> Completed" twins of both, with and without " to <ROOT>/"
#   * real portage ANSI SGR + cursor-move escapes ("\x1b[A", "\x1b[72C") interleaved
# Verbatim tallies of the 304 excerpt lines (counted, not remembered):
#   169 ">>> Jobs:"  ·  28 ">>> Emerging"  ·  28 ">>> Installing"  ·  28 ">>> Completed ("
#   20 of the 28 Emerging lines carry " for <ROOT>/", 8 do not  ·  2 are "0 of 0 complete"
#   23 lines carry at least one ESC byte  ·  every Load avg field is 2-decimal here
#   (the full file also has 1-decimal ones, e.g. "Load avg: 10.1, 28.1, 19.9" at L2308)
# Lines beginning with "#" are this header only; the parser matches nothing on them, which
# the tests assert.


